4d76f584 (205 1793279692018 "guenchi" (("1lwdlzul" . 1) ("o01rj2kt" . 9352)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing g3d") (src . "gfx: a call statement in the shader forms; loop exits only as statements\n\n(call f arg ...) is a statement rendering \"f(arg, ...); \" in both GLSL\ndialects and in WGSL, so a void function -- or one called for its out\nand inout arguments -- can be called; it is spelt out, so an unknown\nhead is still a bad statement.  glsl-check and wgsl-check refuse a call\nwith no function name, and a (break) or (continue) in any expression\nposition, top-level constants included: (set! x (break)) used to render\n\"x = break();\", which the GLSL compiler refuses.\n\nWGSL renames uniform and varying references before it renders, and that\nrenaming no longer reaches the head of a list: a uniform or varying named\ncall, local or fl turned those forms into calls of u.call, u.local or\nu.fl.  A list's head is syntax in these forms, never such a reference.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 774))))
